  "item": {
    "id": 5288921546,
    "number": 71,
    "state": "open",
    "title": "fix(binding): honor explicit zero-valued numeric and climate bounds",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nFix incorrect rotation limits for `number`, `input_number`, and `climate` targets. The previous `_as_float(...) or default` logic treated a valid bound of `0` as missing. The fix falls back only for `None`; missing limits and invalid zero step sizes retain their existing defaults.\n\n**Target:** `main` (stable-line bug fix).\n\n## Reproduction\n\nOn 13 November, @Hinrixx3026 reproduced this with a physical BILRESA wheel:\n\n- Channel 3, Value mode, 10% per notch, 1 s smoothing\n- `input_number` helper: min **-10**, max **0**, step **1**, starting at **-1**\n- One upward notch produced **`Value -1 → 10`** in Live Test, although the maximum is **0**. The helper remained at **-1**.\n\nExpected: `-1 → 0`. The Live Test confirms the incorrect calculation, not that Home Assistant applied the invalid value.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Preserve explicit zero min/max values for numeric and climate rotations.\n- Add a regression test for the observed single-notch failure and tests for boundary handling and missing-limit defaults.\n- Update the English/Czech READMEs, changelog, project status, and hardware test notes.\n\nHistory: **3 commits** — reproducing test, fix/tests, documentation.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [x] Fork CI: **7/7 jobs passed**, including 552 Python tests and 552 against the newer HA test environment: [run 43352202078](https://github.com/Hinrixx3026/ha-ikea-bilresa/actions/runs/43352202078)\n- [x] PR checks on final head `f44ddfd`: required CI and CodeQL passed\n- [x] Original bug reproduced on physical BILRESA\n- [ ] Corrected build tested on physical hardware — **pending**\n\nNo unrelated code changes or private installation identifiers are included. More detailed observations and limitations are in `docs/HARDWARE_TEST.md`.\n\nThanks for the helpful feedback on #59!\n\n*PR text prepared with ChatGPT; hardware test performed by @Hinrixx3026.*",
